      "writtenOn": "2024-01-17T14:41:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "OK. Now that I understand this better, it seems like the reference actually doesn\u0027t add value--either way, we are handling a complete temporary Event object. There\u0027s no existing object that we can cheaply hold a reference to; the iterator is synthesizing Event objects on the fly. It\u0027s _harmless_ to use `const Event\u0026 event` here, because of lifetime extension, but it\u0027s not _beneficial_.\n\nHmm, I guess no complaints.",
